            <value>
               <exData contentType="text/html">
                  <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/"><p style="font-size:9pt;color:#ff0000;text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0in">Obtain the signature of the authorized department administrator and submit the original signed confirmation ticket to 1)<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">  </span>Financial Aid and 2) Payroll Services.</p><p style="font-size:9pt;color:#ff0000;text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0in">If your student is required to sign in with Payroll Services, please make sure the student brings the original, signed confirmation ticket and<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span><span style="font-weight:bold">valid</span>, acceptable documents for proof of eligibility for employment for completion of the I-9 form (complete list of<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">  </span>acceptable documents can be found at<span style="color:#993300"><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></span><span style="color:#3366ff;text-decoration:underline">http://www.uscis.gov/files/form/i-9.pdf</span><span style="color:#993300">)<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></span>to the Payroll Office, College Park Suite 700<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes">  </span>(phone 657-278-2521). The student must complete the sign-in process prior to the student's first day of work. Non-Resident Alien students must submit additional documentation before employment can be approved. Please contact Evajoy Tito at 657-278-8356 for information.<span style="font-weight:bold"> The student may not begin work until he/she has been approved by Payroll.</span></p><p style="font-size:9pt;color:#ff0000;font-weight:bold;text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="font-size:9pt;color:#ff0000;font-style:italic;text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0in">Note: If the Social Security card is used for the completion of the I-9, the student must present to Payroll the original Social Security card.</p></body>
               </exData>
            </value>
            <font typeface="Myriad Pro"/>
            <margin topInset="0.5mm" bottomInset="0.5mm" leftInset="0.5mm" rightInset="0.5mm"/>
         </draw>
